# Pitch channel reversal for the FS-i6 on this airframe.
#
# Measured 2026-09-02 by check_stick_sense.py, and confirmed in the air first:
# pushing the pitch stick forward flew the aircraft BACKWARD.
#
#   pitch stick fully forward -> ch2 1777, trim 1481, so +296 us
#   RC2_REV +1                -> control_in POSITIVE
#   positive pitch            -> NOSE UP -> flies BACKWARD
#
# The FS-i6's elevator output runs opposite to what ArduPilot expects. Nothing
# in preflight.py can see this: a reversed channel and a correct one produce
# identical PWM ranges, and self-levelling comes from the IMU so the aircraft
# still hovers perfectly. Only the SIGN relative to trim separates them.
#
# Roll measured correct in the same run (+313 us -> flies right), which is what
# rules out a board mounted 180 degrees round -- that reverses BOTH axes and is
# fixed with AHRS_ORIENTATION, never by reversing channels.
RC2_REV -1
